  "note": "Triennial election of the councillors of Londonderry Corporation, polled Wednesday 17 May 1967 on the three wards of 1936 (North, South, Waterside); 32 candidates for 15 councillors' seats (Derry Journal, 5 May 1967, p. 1). Result declared at 12.30 a.m. on 18 May. Barry McLaughlin's vote (2,396) is the News-Letter's; it agrees with the Journal's printed Labour total of 14,174. Mrs. Harrigan was the first woman member of the council for over 40 years (Derry Journal)."
